1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,835
This robot has no pinky.

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:02,974
On purpose.

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:04,440
Boston Dynamics says

4
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,840
its engineers taped their
ring and pinky fingers

5
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,024
together for a day.

6
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,007
The verdict?

7
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,010
Leave it out.

8
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,400
Atlas’s new hand

9
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:12,520
has four digits,

10
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,254
but thirteen
degrees of freedom.

11
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,054
Independent ways to move.

12
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,080
The company says it can pinch,

13
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,167
turn objects, and
press tool triggers.

14
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,560
A fifth digit would mean

15
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,978
three more actuators.

16
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,144
More cost.

17
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:24,981
More bulk.

18
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,192
More things to break.

19
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:29,443
So the goal is a
useful, reliable hand.

20
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,156
Looking human is optional.

21
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,574
Apparently, even
robots have a budget.
